  "body": "## What\n`src/board.rs` becomes real (plan \u00a73.3), with the CLI glue the skeleton's `bf claim|heartbeat|release|note|board` arms call:\n- **Storage**: `~/.bf/bf.sqlite` (or `$BF_DATA_DIR`), one append-only `board` table with immutability triggers, `jobs` (for PR 9), `inbox_seen`. WAL, 2 s busy timeout, IMMEDIATE transactions with bounded retry. No hub, no lock: any agent shell writes one short transaction.\n- **Claims**: repo-relative paths (dir ends with `/`; `dir/**` accepted as `dir/`; `..`/absolute/globs rejected); overlap = component-wise prefix; conflict \u2192 exit 2 naming holder, id, expiry and intent; identical re-claim by the same agent is idempotent; default TTL 30 m, max 3 h.\n- **Heartbeat/release**: `expires_at = now + ttl`; heartbeat or release on an expired claim \u2192 `STALE` (exit 2). `bf release <id> --proof '<cmd>'` runs the command in the claim's repo (15-min cap, 1 MiB capture, own process group) and records `exit`, `sha256` of output, `git status --porcelain` paths and `HEAD`.\n- **Notes**: `--to <agent> | --re <claim> | --pr <url>`; unaddressed notes are \u2264 280-byte status lines. `bf board --to me` prints the caller's inbox; every write prints `N note(s) addressed to you` while unread.\n- **Identity**: `--as`/`BF_AGENT` declared name plus the observed provider/pid from `/proc` (PR 4's `identity.rs`).\n- **Digest**: every write and `bf board` atomically regenerate `~/.bf/AGENT_CHAT.md` (`# BulletFarm board \u2014 GENERATED \u2026`, active claims, recent 30, `<!-- bf:end -->`); hand-written lines after the marker are imported as `legacy-md` notes. The \"Live agents\" section is filled by the discovery PR.\n\n## Acceptance (plan \u00a74, PR 5) \u2014 `tests/cli_board.rs`, black-box via the binary\n`claim src/ -m a --as codex-1` \u2192 0 \u00b7 `claim src/api.rs -m b --as claude-orch` \u2192 2 naming `codex-1`/`c-1` \u00b7 `release c-1 --proof 'true'` \u2192 0 with `exit 0` \u00b7 second claim \u2192 0 \u00b7 repeat release \u2192 2 (stale) \u00b7 addressed note + `board --to claude-orch` \u00b7 digest header + `c-` \u00b7 straggler after end marker \u2192 `legacy-md` \u00b7 `--ttl 9h` \u2192 64 \u00b7 `$HOME/.bf` created 0700.\nLocal: fmt/clippy `-D warnings` clean; `cargo test` lib 17 + cli_board 2 + cli_skeleton 5 + core 3; `bash scripts/check` EXIT 0 (17 s isolated).\n\nThe host transition (install, archive the current AGENT_CHAT.md, symlink) is a separate operator step recorded on the board after merge \u2014 not in this PR.\n\n## Review\nReviewer must be a different vendor (grok, codex or cursor): `REVIEW: approve <head-sha>` via `gh pr review --comment`, then `gh pr merge --rebase --delete-branch`.\n\nbf-author: claude/claude-orch \u00b7 bf-claim: AGENT_CHAT.md 2026-09-18T16:34Z\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
